.TH AGENT-HOOK-POST-EDIT 1 "2026-06-30" "agentguard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
agent-hook-post-edit \- format and lint edited files through Sley
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent-hook-post-edit
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B agent-hook-post-edit
reads an agent edit hook JSON payload from standard input and delegates changed
files to
.BR "sley hook format --stdin" ,
one batch per directory (with a per-file
.BR "sley hook format-file"
fallback for older Sley installs).
It then passes every edited file to
.BR "sley hook lint --stdin" ,
the same checks the commit gate runs, and returns its findings (exit status 1)
as agent context, bounded to the first 40 lines, so lint and schema errors
surface at edit time, even in files no commit checks.
Lint covers whole files, so findings can predate the edit.
Lint that cannot run is not reported.
Commit readiness and verification remain native commit-hook responsibilities
so human and agent commit workflows share the same readiness path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Formatting completed, selected formatter failures were ignored after Sley
surfaced them, or no format target was selected.
Lint findings do not change the exit status.
.TP
.B 2
The local install is missing required dependencies such as
.BR sley .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR agent-hook-pre-edit (1),
.BR sley (1)
